1. One article is added after Article 177 of the Criminal Law as Article 177a: “Whoever, under any of the following circumstances, obstructs the management of credit cards shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention and/or shall be fined not less than 10,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan; if the amount is huge or if there are other serious circumstances, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years and shall be fined not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan:
“(1) knowingly holds or transports counterfeit credit cards, or knowingly holds or transports counterfeit blank credit cards, in relatively large quantities;
“(2) illegally holds credit cards of another person in relatively large quantities;
“(3) obtains credit cards by fraud using false identity certificates;
“(4) sells, purchases, or provides another person with counterfeit credit cards or with credit cards obtained by fraud using false identity certificates.
“Whoever steals, buys, or illegally provides another person with the information or materials concerning the credit cards of another person shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph.
“Any employee of a bank or any other financial institution who takes advantage of his position to commit the crime mentioned in the preceding paragraph shall be subjected to a severe punishment.”

2. Article 196 of the Criminal Law is amended to read: “Whoever commits credit card fraud under any of the following circumstances, if the amount involved is relatively large, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention and shall be fined not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan; if the amount is huge or if there are other serious circumstances, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than ten years and shall be fined not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan; if the amount is especially huge or if there are other especially serious circumstances, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years or life imprisonment and shall be fined not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan or shall have his property confiscated:
“(1) using a counterfeit credit card or using a credit card obtained by fraud with a false identity certificate;
“(2) using an invalidated credit card;
“(3) fraudulently using another person's credit card;
“(4) malicious overdraft.
“For the purpose of the preceding paragraph, 'malicious overdraft' means the act of a cardholder who, for the purpose of illegal possession, overdrafts beyond the prescribed limit or within the prescribed time limit and still does not return the overdrawn amount after being urged by the issuing bank.
“Whoever steals a credit card and uses it shall be convicted and punished in accordance with the provisions of Article 264 of this Law.”
